0 161 660 [
[(Octave Doubling via Variable Comb Filter)]
] 19 -0 0.5 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 190 219 [
[(We already saw how to use ring modulation to alias a pitched sound)]
[(down one octave. Here we do the reverse: filter out all odd)]
[(harmonics using a variable-delay comb filter tuned one octave above)]
[(the incoming sound. We use two taps into the delay line. The fixed)]
[(one \050[delread~]\051 adjusts for the delayed output of [sigmund~]. The)]
[(variable one \050[delread4~]\051 adds to this an additional delay equal)]
[(to 1/2 the measured period of the incoming sound. These two are)]
[(added. Odd harmonics are 180 degrees out of phase at the two taps)]
[(and cancel. Even harmonics get through - so the sound goes up an)]
[(octave, without denaturing the timbre as a speed-up would.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
